  "priorExpiration": "2006-02-19",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 203.01 Waiver of Rules.\n\n(a) The commission or the presiding officer shall waive the provisions of any of the commission’s administrative rules, except when precluded by statute, in response to a motion filed by an interested party, or on the commission or presiding officer’s own motion, if it is found that:\n\n(1) The waiver serves the public interest; and\n\n(2) The waiver will not disrupt the orderly and efficient resolution of matters before the commission.\n\n(b) In determining the public interest, the commission or the presiding officer shall find a request to be in the public interest if:\n\n(1) Compliance with the rule would be onerous or inapplicable given the circumstances of the affected person; or\n\n(2) The purpose of the rule would be satisfied by an alternative method proposed.\n\n(c) Any person affected by a rule and seeking a waiver shall file a written motion, except as provided in (d) below.\n\n(d) The commission or the presiding officer shall consider any waiver request made orally during a hearing or prehearing conference.\n\n(e) A request for a waiver shall specify the basis for the waiver, how the waiver might affect other parties or participants, and a proposed alternative, if any.\n\nSource. #2011, eff 5-4-82; ss by #2912, eff 11-26-84; ss by #4998, eff 11-26-90; ss by #6365, INTERIM, eff 11-18-96, EXPIRED: 3-18-97\n\nNew. #6559, eff 8-19-97, EXPIRED: 8-19-05\n\nNew. #8420, INTERIM, eff 8-23-05, EXPIRED: 2-19-06\n\nNew. #8657-A, eff 6-10-06\n\nNew. #14184, eff 1-24-25 (formerly Puc 201.05)",
